I can't confirm a 90-day deadline. I just checked the live Nevada guide, and it still says **30 days**.

**What the guide currently says:**
- **Deadline:** The landlord has 30 days after the tenancy ends and the tenant moves out to return the deposit or send an itemized written list of deductions.
- **Deposit cap:** 3 months' rent, counting all security together (including prepaid last month's rent and any surety bond).
- **Penalty for wrongful withholding:** The full deposit, plus court-ordered damages of up to the same amount again (up to 2x total).
- **Move-in record:** Written leases must provide for a signed record of the unit's inventory and condition.

**Source:** [PropInspect Nevada guide](https://propinspect.net/security-deposit-laws/nevada), last reviewed **October 12, 2026**, based on [Nevada Revised Statutes § 118A.242](https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-118A.html#NRS118ASec242).

